{title: Rock of My Heart}
{subtitle: Psalms 73:26}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 78}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] |
| [Bb] | [F/A] | [Gm7] | [Eb] | ×2

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]I am always with you [F/A]held by your hand
[Gm7]Guided by counsel toward [Eb]the promised land
[Bb]In the heaven above I [F/A]have no one else
On the [Eb]earth below you [F]are my wealth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My [Bb]flesh and my heart may [F]fail
But [Gm7]God is the rock of my [Eb]heart
[Bb]My portion forever [F]remains
[Cm7]The strength within [F7sus4]my [Bb]frail
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Those who are far from you will [F/A]perish
[Gm7]Destroying all who are un[Eb]faithful
[Bb]But as for me it is [F/A]good to be near
[Eb]Refuge in the Lord I [F]find
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]I tell of all your works [F]with [Gm7]joy
[Eb]Near God my spirit finds [F]its [Gm7]home
[Eb]No fear remains [F]when [Gm7]I am close
Your [Cm7]light upon the [Fsus4]world is shown
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
My [Bb]flesh and my heart may [F/A]fail
But [Gm7]God is the rock of my [Eb]heart
[Bb]My portion forever [F]remains
[Cm7]The strength within [F7sus4]my [Bb]frail
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
God is [F/A]my portion for[Gm7]ever
My [Eb]rock and my strength [Bb]
{end_of_verse}
